RC-WR04 log: rollback (fault exit-after-daemon v1.8.1) with the result write failing; post-fix rig builds of 83df1e1f
--- notes.txt
Blocker: before the click (07:07, N running), update-result.json was made a directory holding one file
(keep). WriteResult makes its temp file in the config folder, then renames it onto the result path; the
rename onto a non-empty directory fails, so only the result write fails. The N+1 GUI's TakeResult cannot
remove a non-empty directory, so it stayed for the installer. No chmod: the config folder also holds
daemon.sock, daemon.log and update.log, and its mode was never changed (drwx------ admin:staff before
and after).

Fresh viewers: the first try at 07:08:32 used the installed 1.8.0 CLI without --keep-daemon. That CLI
asked the 1.8.1 daemon for a takeover and the downgrade wall refused it (daemon.log 07:08:32 "refused a
takeover from build v1.8.0"; same as the R2-B capture note in 18-07); the sessions were unaffected. The
helper then blocked on its FIFO write until it was killed at 07:27:43. Later viewers use
`attach --keep-daemon` (cli-keep.exp).

Session output stall (OBSERVED, cause not established): the first --keep-daemon viewers at 07:28:19 and
07:28:25 replayed tickA up to TICK 228 and vimB up to VTICK 234. Both tickers started about 07:07:35 and
tick once a second, so both stopped producing output at about 07:11:25 and stayed stopped until about
07:28:24. The shells and vim kept their pids throughout. Ticks are gapless across the stall, so the
processes were held (blocked), not killed or restarted. Output resumed right after a viewer joined:
TICK 281 at 07:29:18, TICK 950 at 07:40:37 (669 ticks in 679 s), VTICK 964 at 07:40:42. A 2 s monitor
(the ticker shell's sleep child, plus the queued bytes on unix sockets) ran 07:29:57-07:40:54 and saw no
second stall and 0 queued bytes. daemon.log has no line between 07:08:32 and 07:28:19. Nothing the rig
did lines up with 07:11:25: the last click was 07:07:47, and the hung helper never connected to the
daemon. Display sleep is 0 and the screensaver idle time is 0 in this guest. Not a WR-04 criterion
(shells kept, same pids, under the 1.8.1 daemon). Reported for a follow-up soak test.
